    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Each part expands two brackets with numeric multipliers and then collects like terms. The extra demand over a single expansion is the subtraction sign: -3(x+1) gives -3x-3, and in part c -2(x-4) gives -2x+8. That is a sign decision and a collecting step, but all the linear terms are signposted by the instruction. It is clearly harder than p13-q4's single direct expansions. It stays below p15-q12 and p18-q8, which use monomial multipliers or a multi-step, explain-why chain.",
